# Precomputed data cache — fast to regenerate (py -3 precompute.py ALL),
# not worth versioning (unlike RCTBE's HMM precompute, which IS committed
# there because a 10-15 min walk-forward refit per asset is genuinely
# expensive to redo).
mr_precomputed_*.parquet

# Search working state — regenerable from a resumed/rerun search.
# top_strategies.json is the one file worth committing deliberately if a
# specific result is worth preserving (not gitignored by the line below).
meanreversion_output*/run.log
meanreversion_output*/checkpoint.json
meanreversion_output*/checkpoint.json.tmp
meanreversion_output*/DONE
meanreversion_output*/results.csv
meanreversion_output_stale_*/

# Raw/consolidated market data staged for ad-hoc diagnostics (e.g. via the
# device bridge) — large, regenerable from the Dukascopy cache, same
# reasoning as mr_precomputed_*.parquet above.
data/

# video_strategy_backtest.py's own sweep run log + raw per-draw CSV —
# regenerable by re-running the sweep. video_strategy_top_candidates.json
# IS worth versioning (same "small result worth preserving" convention as
# top_strategies.json above), so it's deliberately NOT listed here. Glob
# (not an exact name) since ad-hoc runs get suffixed, e.g. sweep_log_3yr.txt
# for the 2022/2024/2026 version.
sweep_log*.txt
video_strategy_sweep_results*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# vps_full_review.py's incremental resume checkpoint — regenerable by
# re-running the script (it resumes from results.json's own length, but
# the checkpoint and results file are identical in content by design;
# only the results.json is worth versioning as a preserved finding).
vps_full_review_checkpoint.json

